  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Islet Lighthouse",
    "description": "A striped lighthouse on a rocky islet of its own, its lantern lighting up above the waves at night to guide ships home. A wooden jetty runs out to the south, and a small sailboat is on its way in. 37 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Island** — four grey Block 2x2s make a 4x4 islet, two blocks high. Rocks ring the waterline, with a gap on the south side for the jetty, and two more sit on top at the back corners.\n2. **Jetty** — a wooden Plate 2x4 runs south from the islet. Its far end stands on two Cube pilings; its near end meets the islet between two rocks, and a Half Cube makes a step up onto the island. A Barrel waits at the end.\n3. **Tower** — three Block 2x2s stacked white, red, white. The Door faces the jetty; a Small Window looks south from the red band and another north from the top.\n4. **Gallery** — a Slab 4x4 caps the tower and overhangs it by one on every side. Two Beams make the front and back railing, and two Short Beams, turned 90° (press **R**), the sides.\n5. **Lantern** — two Lanterns stacked in the middle of the gallery, under a Round Plate 2x2 and a red Cone Roof. In World View they light up at night.\n6. **Boat** — a Plate 2x4 hull, a Post for the mast and a Large Window, turned 90°, for the sail.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Island: 4 Block 2x2, 10 Rock\n- Jetty: 1 Plate 2x4, 2 Cube, 1 Half Cube, 1 Barrel\n- Tower: 3 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 2 Small Window\n- Gallery: 1 Slab 4x4, 2 Beam, 2 Short Beam\n- Lantern: 2 Lantern, 1 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Cone Roof\n- Boat: 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Post, 1 Large Window\n\n37 bricks in all.\n",
